4.164.m:
Those who give well-tilled earth to the best of the twice-born go to the abode of Śakra, their bodies utterly purified;
those who take it away through sheer force, lust, or greed do not escape from the unfathomable depths of Raurava hell.
Description of the Rite of the Gift of the Earth

4.165.m:
Yudhiṣṭhira said:
The gift of land is appropriate for kṣatriyas, not for others;
for they are able to acquire, give, and protect [it].

4.175.m:
There is none higher than Brahmā, Īśa, and Keśava to be worshipped, nor is there any sacrifice equal to the horse sacrifice;
there is no sacred bathing place equal to the Gaṅgā even in the three worlds, nor is there any gift in this world equal to the Tulāpuruṣa.
Description of the rite of the golden embryo gift

4.176.m:
Yudhiṣṭhira said:
O Blessed One, Lord of all beings, worshipped by all beings,
for the grace of all worlds, tell me another [rite],

Yudhiṣṭhira said:
Declare its procedure, O Lord of gods, O Eternal One;
with what dimensions and how this is to be given, O Supreme Lord.

4.177.m:
Brahmā said:
'While ruling the kingdom, O earth-ruler, your limbs were nourished;
but nothing abundant was given by you, devoted as you were to the doctrine of the Self.

4.178.m:
The blessed Kṛṣṇa said:
Formerly, the blessed Śaṅkara had contracted marriage with Umā;
rejoicing with her, he remained for many groups of years.

The Blessed One said:
'From now on, O gods, I shall remain with upward-drawn semen;
and I shall stay like a pillar; and this will be my name.'

4.179.m:
Yudhiṣṭhira said:
